      <span class="zczp-subtitle">Understanding ZCZP</span>
      <h2 class="zczp-title">
        What Is a ZCZP Instrument on the Social Stock Exchange?
      </h2>
      <div class="zczp-desc">
        <p>
          A Zero Coupon Zero Principal (ZCZP) instrument is a SEBI-approved
          security listed on India's Social Stock Exchange that allows you to
          contribute to registered NGOs without expecting financial repayment.
          Your entire investment goes towards funding specific social programmes
          run by SSE-listed not-for-profit organisations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Instead of interest or principal, you receive structured, audited
          impact reports that show what changed because of your capital:
          beneficiaries reached, programmes implemented, and outcomes delivered.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

